verified.evidence:
`run()` calls `hb = registry.beat(run_dir, 0)` (probe_eval.py:565), then `hb.emit(0, total_events, "item")` once (probe_eval.py:576), then nothing until `hb.finish()` (probe_eval.py:668). No `emit` advances `done`. Every heartbeat file of today's four eval runs holds exactly two lines with `done: 0`, e.g. /net/tokyo100-10g/data/str01_01/y-guo/reproduce/new1/outputs/debug/eval/f343c9118516/heartbeat/0-0.jsonl:
  {"done": 0, "total": 16, "unit": "item", "ts": 1789885103.3302355}
  {"done": 0, "total": 16, "unit": "item", "ts": 1789885103.4417381, "status": "done"}
`run.py ls --debug` accordingly prints `eval-f343c9118516 ... status=ok progress=0/16 item rate=0/s` for a run whose probe_report.json, fires.parquet and done.json are all on disk. Contracts 8.4 (notes/plans/2026-09-17-contracts.md) pins the opposite: "Every batch piece opens its file with registry.beat(run_dir, piece) and emits emit(0, total, unit) before its main loop ... then one beat per unit of work, then finish()". The other three one-process stages do beat per unit: data/build_training_dataset.py:99 (`hb.emit(i + 1, len(pairs), "row")`), eval/score_run.py:209 (`hb.emit(i, len(pairs), "task")`), agent/run_tasks.py:203. eval is the only stage that does not.
